  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Luca Cordero di Montezemolo joined Ferrari as Enzo Ferrari’s assistant and quickly became team manager, helping the marque return to Formula One championship success. After senior roles across Fiat’s publishing and consumer businesses, he returned to Ferrari as chairman in 1991. Over the next two decades he oversaw a revival in road-car competitiveness and a sustained run of racing titles.\n\nBeyond Ferrari, Montezemolo chaired Fiat, Confindustria and Alitalia while building ventures outside the motor industry. He co-founded Italy’s private high-speed rail operator Italo and developed Charme Capital Partners as an international private-equity platform. His current portfolio combines chairmanship of Italo Holding and Charme with Manifatture Sigaro Toscano and Telethon, the genetic-disease research charity he has led since 2009.",
